{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long gcd_ex(long long a, long long b) {\n    if (a < b) swap(a, b);\n    while (b != 0) {\n        long long r = a % b;\n        a = b;\n        b = r;\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nlong long lcm_ex(long long a, long long b) {\n    return a / gcd_ex(a, b) * b;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    \n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    if (y <= n) {\n        long long g = gcd_ex(x, y);\n        for (; g > 1; g = gcd_ex(x, y)) {\n            x /= g;\n            y /= g;\n        }\n        cout << x << \"/\" << y;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    long long best_n = 0, best_d = 1;\n    long double min_delta = numeric_limits<long double>::max();\n    \n    for (long long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        long long L = lcm_ex(d, y);\n        long long T = x * (L / y);\n        long long step = L / d;\n        \n        long long candidate1 = T / step;\n        long long v1 = candidate1 * step;\n        long double diff1 = fabsl((long double)T - v1) / L;\n        \n        if (diff1 < min_delta) {\n            min_delta = diff1;\n            best_n = candidate1;\n            best_d = d;\n        }\n        \n        long long candidate2 = (T + step - 1) / step;\n        long long v2 = candidate2 * step;\n        long double diff2 = fabsl((long double)T - v2) / L;\n        \n        if (diff2 < min_delta) {\n            min_delta = diff2;\n            best_n = candidate2;\n            best_d = d;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    long long g = gcd_ex(best_n, best_d);\n    best_n /= g;\n    best_d /= g;\n    \n    cout << best_n << \"/\" << best_d;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef gcd_ex(a, b):\n    if a < b:\n        a, b = b, a\n    while b != 0:\n        r = a % b\n        a = b\n        b = r\n    return a\n\ndef lcm_ex(a, b):\n    return a // gcd_ex(a, b) * b\n\ndef main():\n    x, y, n = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    \n    if y <= n:\n        g = gcd_ex(x, y)\n        while g > 1:\n            x //= g\n            y //= g\n            g = gcd_ex(x, y)\n        print(f\"{x}/{y}\")\n        return\n    \n    best_n = 0\n    best_d = 1\n    min_delta = float('inf')\n    \n    for d in range(1, n + 1):\n        L = lcm_ex(d, y)\n        T = x * (L // y)\n        step = L // d\n        \n        candidate1 = T // step\n        v1 = candidate1 * step\n        diff1 = abs(T - v1) / L\n        \n        if diff1 < min_delta:\n            min_delta = diff1\n            best_n = candidate1\n            best_d = d\n        \n        candidate2 = (T + step - 1) // step\n        v2 = candidate2 * step\n        diff2 = abs(T - v2) / L\n        \n        if diff2 < min_delta:\n            min_delta = diff2\n            best_n = candidate2\n            best_d = d\n    \n    g = gcd_ex(best_n, best_d)\n    best_n //= g\n    best_d //= g\n    \n    print(f